      "content": "That's a good start, I like the tension. But honestly, it feels a bit too polite for a private conversation between two guys like that. In 1954, even if they're \"refined\" business owners, they weren't necessarily using metaphors like \"the dance\" all the time. They'd be much more blunt about who they don't want in their shops or on their streets. \n\nCan you rewrite the scene to be more visceral? I want to see the actual way they'd talk about the racial tensions—the specific ways they'd describe the people they're excluding. I'm not looking for a cartoonish villain, just the raw, unvarnished way people spoke back then when they were being honest about their prejudices. Make it feel more gritty and real.",
